  "final_response": "I have fixed the bug in `app/parser.py`. \n\n**Description of the change:**\nIn the `parse_date` function, the code was unpacking the date parts as `year, day, month`, which incorrectly swapped the month and the day (e.g. \"2026-03-07\" evaluated to a tuple of `(2026, 7, 3)` instead of `(2026, 3, 7)`). I corrected the unpacking order to `year, month, day` so that it accurately matches the `\"YYYY-MM-DD\"` format. The `test_dates` test now passes successfully.",
